Chapters:
00:00 Cognitive Debt
02:37 Debt as Leverage
09:22 Abstraction vs Understanding
16:27 Humans as Monitors

Sources:
Geoffrey Litt, "Understanding is the new bottleneck": https://www.geoffreylitt.com/2026/07/...
Simon Willison, "Understand to participate": https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/2/...
Simon Willison link-blog note on cognitive debt: https://simonwillison.net/2026/Feb/15...
Margaret-Anne Storey, "How Generative and Agentic AI Shift Concern from Technical Debt to Cognitive Debt": https://margaretstorey.com/blog/2026/...
Margaret-Anne Storey, "From Technical Debt to Cognitive and Intent Debt": https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.22106
Peter Naur, "Programming as Theory Building": https://pages.cs.wisc.edu/~remzi/Naur...
Lisanne Bainbridge, "The Ironies of Automation": https://ckrybus.com/static/papers/Bai...

My related writing:
AI Coding: From Tactics to Strategy: https://vivekhaldar.com/articles/ai-c...
